-- The lobby: a closed-off corner of a dead mall (docs/plans/lobby-rework.md,
-- "The place"; the owner, 2026-10-15). LB1a's grey-box layout, for walking
-- and judging distances before anything is modelled: World/MallBuilder
-- builds it, Logic/MallLayout checks it.
--
-- Studs, on the floor plan from the court's middle: x east, z south (the
-- spawn looks north at the video store), y up from the court floor. A room
-- is {x0, z0, x1, z1}; each builds its own walls just inside its rectangle.
-- A door stands on the line two rooms share (`runs` is the way that line
-- goes) and cuts both their walls; one with no `b` opens to outside and is
-- filled (`fill`).
--
-- The hall reads end to end: the diner closes its west end (the owner's
-- place for it), the giant shutter its east end, where the dead mall goes
-- on in the dark behind the grille. The video store's back door is the
-- only way into the garage, where the squads leave.

